  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Skyclarys (omaveloxolone). Version: 1; Original: 06/30/2023; Accepted: 09/15/2023; Effective: 11/1/2023.",
    "Encoded: closed Friedreich\u2019s ataxia indication, approval criteria 1\u20137 and separate denial criteria 2\u20134. Denial 1 is failure to meet approval criteria.",
    "Clinically symptomatic examples: impaired coordination, diminished reflexes, frequent falls, skeletal muscle weakness.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor ALT, AST and total bilirubin prior to initiation, every month for the first three months of treatment, and periodically thereafter. Avoid concomitant use with moderate or strong CYP3A4 inducers or inhibitors. May cause fetal harm.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 6 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 102 capsules per 34 days.",
    "Genetic testing, symptoms, mFARS score and baseline laboratory documentation require manual review; categorical attestations encode the stated requirements and inclusive thresholds. Monitoring, cautions, duration and quantity remain notes only, so this pack remains partial.",
    "PDL status remains unknown. No evaluate-linked alternatives are specified."
  ],
